# Environment variables. Copy to `.env` for local work, or paste the values into
# Vercel under Settings -> Environment Variables. `.env` is gitignored, this file
# is not, so the shape of what is needed can be committed without the values.
#
# Nothing here is required for the site to work.
#
# The viewer badge hides itself when these are absent, which is the intended
# failure: a portfolio should not show an error because a counter is not
# configured. Everything else - all nine sections, the resume, the chat - is
# static and needs no backend at all.
#
# The endpoint answers 200 with `{"count":0,"available":false}` rather than an
# error status in that case. That is deliberate: a failed request logs a console
# error, and Lighthouse's `errors-in-console` audit fails on any failed request,
# which cost Best Practices a point on a site with nothing else wrong with it.
# See the `unavailable()` helper in api/viewers.js.

# --- presence badge (/api/viewers) ------------------------------------------
#
# Exactly two variables are read, at api/viewers.js:
#
#   KV_REST_API_URL      the REST endpoint
#   KV_REST_API_TOKEN    the REST token
#
# Set them by hand under Settings -> Environment Variables, or let an
# integration create them.
#
# IMPORTANT: the names come from the Custom Prefix on the integration's connect
# step, not from the provider. Vercel's "Upstash for Redis" integration offers
# `STORAGE` as the default prefix, which would create `STORAGE_URL` and
# `STORAGE_TOKEN` - neither of which is read here, with no error to explain why.
# Set the prefix to `KV_REST_API`. Connecting with the default was almost the
# mistake that would have looked like a broken badge rather than a naming
# mismatch.
#
# Connecting an integration also creates three more that this project ignores:
# `KV_REST_API_REDIS_URL`, `KV_REST_API_KV_URL`, `KV_REST_API_READ_ONLY_TOKEN`.
# They are harmless. Deleting them saves nothing.
#
#   Vercel:  Storage -> Create Database -> Upstash for Redis
#            prefix the connect step with KV_REST_API
#   Upstash: console.upstash.com -> Database -> REST API, copy both values
#
# Note "Global Config" is NOT a substitute. It is an edge-middleware config store
# read through the `@vercel/global-config` SDK, with no Redis REST endpoint. The
# sorted-set commands this function issues - ZADD, ZCARD, ZREMRANGEBYSCORE,
# ZREM, EXPIRE - do not exist there.
#
# After adding or changing either variable, redeploy. They are read when the
# function starts, so an already-running deployment keeps reporting presence as
# unavailable until it is replaced.

KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-database.upstash.io
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=your-rest-token